  "desc": "ρ BLACK HOLE · physics fork. JH 2026-05-20 \"do a fork of this that attempts to make the black hole more mathematically and physically based with the center accretion disk not just a circle but a proper black hole math like interstellar - find example science code\". Replaces the parent's layered 2D pipeline (back-wrap arcs / lensing halo / photon ring) with a single Schwarzschild geodesic ray-tracer. buildGeodesicTable() runs RK4 on the Binet equation u'' + u = (3/2)·u² with 512 samples in b ∈ [b_photon·1.0001, 18 rs] (b_photon = 3√3/2 ≈ 2.598 rs); flags rays captured when u exceeds 2 (deep inside photon sphere), records α = φ_exit − π otherwise. Per-pixel back-trace bends each ray to the accretion-disk plane (basis built from bh.phi + DISK_INCLINATION_DEG), samples a Shakura-Sunyaev T(r) ∝ r^-3/4 disk with hash-noise stripe texture, Doppler beaming (δ³ luminance + hue shift, β = β_max·√(rIn/r) Keplerian), and gravitational redshift √(1 − rs/r). Renders to a PHYSICS_SCALE-scaled offscreen ImageData (default 0.42), drawImage-blits to the main canvas. Reference: James 2015 arXiv:1502.03808 (DNGR). Approximations vs full Kerr DNGR: Schwarzschild (non-spinning), single-pass deflection in the ray–BH plane, single disk intersection (no higher-order images), HSL ramp instead of blackbody. Parent's lifecycle (growing→dissolving→idle, cycle escalator, starfield, glass logo, controls panel) preserved · physics replaces the BH visual layer only. JH 2026-05-21 sweep 6: DISK_INCLINATION_DEG 82°→28° per \"still doesn't have any front facing disk\" · disk now tilts toward the viewer (between EHT M87's ~17° and Interstellar's ~80°) so the bright annulus reads as a face-on ring around the EH shadow with the lensed far-side wrap arcing up over it.",
